1
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:04,609
Police found her in the street.
Looks like she was bitten.

2
00:01:04,778 --> 00:01:06,128
Some kind of an animal.

3
00:01:06,321 --> 00:01:08,154
Jesus! Her water’s broken!

4
00:01:08,323 --> 00:01:10,037
She's going into
uterine contractions!

5
00:01:10,159 --> 00:01:12,204
We'll have to do a C-section!

6
00:02:10,469 --> 00:02:11,953
What you got down there,
little man?

7
00:02:12,095 --> 00:02:13,802
Oh, that's my heatseeker.

8
00:02:13,902 --> 00:02:15,356
I'll bet it is.

9
00:02:18,602 --> 00:02:19,893
So, where are we going?

10
00:02:20,062 --> 00:02:21,715
It's a surprise, baby.

11
00:02:21,855 --> 00:02:23,563
Yeah, I like surprises.

12
00:02:30,030 --> 00:02:31,405
Oh, my God!

13
00:02:31,823 --> 00:02:34,528
What the fuck are we doing here?

14
00:02:37,210 --> 00:02:38,575
Look at all that.

15
00:02:41,463 --> 00:02:42,917
What the fuck is that?

16
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:55,510
What did you just say?

17
00:03:34,511 --> 00:03:35,511
Wow.

18
00:03:51,069 --> 00:03:52,232
What's up?

19
00:03:52,654 --> 00:03:54,196
Man!

20
00:04:04,499 --> 00:04:05,698
All right.

21
00:04:30,817 --> 00:04:32,857
What's happening?

22
00:04:39,576 --> 00:04:41,070
Whoa!

23
00:04:41,495 --> 00:04:42,775
Man.

24
00:04:47,751 --> 00:04:48,949
Fuck.

25
00:04:59,972 --> 00:05:01,632
Fuck. I need a drink.

26
00:05:57,404 --> 00:05:59,278
What's wrong, baby?

27
00:06:55,254 --> 00:06:56,254
Is that him?

28
00:06:56,672 --> 00:06:58,166
Jesus, that's him.

29
00:06:58,590 --> 00:07:01,377
It's Blade. It's the Daywalker.

30
00:07:23,240 --> 00:07:24,520
Come on, Daywalker!

31
00:07:45,095 --> 00:07:47,966
I'm gonna rip
your fucking head off!

32
00:08:42,152 --> 00:08:44,359
That's him! Get him!

33
00:08:44,780 --> 00:08:45,780
Fuck him up!

34
00:08:46,073 --> 00:08:49,157
We're gonna jack you up.
Make him hurt bad.

35
00:09:54,433 --> 00:09:55,678
Quinn...

36
00:09:59,021 --> 00:10:00,861
I'm getting a little tired
of chopping you up.

37
00:10:05,402 --> 00:10:09,234
Thought I might try fire
for a change.

38
00:10:11,909 --> 00:10:14,197
Give my regards to Frost.

39
00:10:18,123 --> 00:10:19,368
Please don't!

40
00:10:33,889 --> 00:10:35,051
Put him out.

41
00:10:35,474 --> 00:10:37,098
- Yes, sir.
- Paramedics.

42
00:11:00,165 --> 00:11:03,415
Got a charred cadaver for you.
Still warm, too.

43
00:11:03,835 --> 00:11:05,495
One, two, three.

44
00:11:10,467 --> 00:11:12,543
Jesus, that's rank.

45
00:11:13,637 --> 00:11:16,093
He was still screaming
when they found him...

46
00:11:16,515 --> 00:11:19,220
stapled to a wall.

47
00:11:19,643 --> 00:11:20,923
That's very pretty.

48
00:11:34,533 --> 00:11:35,693
Did you check the chem count?

49
00:11:36,076 --> 00:11:37,654
Blood sugar's
three times norm...

50
00:11:38,078 --> 00:11:39,831
phosphorus and uric acid
are off the charts.

51
00:11:39,931 --> 00:11:41,740
You took this off a DOA?

52
00:11:45,794 --> 00:11:47,703
But this doesn't make any sense.

53
00:11:51,425 --> 00:11:53,667
The red blood cells are
biconvex, which is impossible.

54
00:11:54,094 --> 00:11:56,134
Look at the polys,
they're binucleated.

55
00:12:00,642 --> 00:12:03,477
Curtis,
it's 3.00 in the morning...

56
00:12:03,896 --> 00:12:04,896
This is not a joke.

57
00:12:05,188 --> 00:12:07,062
I've got the body
in the morgue right now.

58
00:12:08,984 --> 00:12:11,440
I thought you promised
to give me some distance.

59
00:12:12,487 --> 00:12:14,610
I just want you to come down
and take a look.

60
00:12:21,079 --> 00:12:24,413
Show me the body.

61
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:27,040
And I don’t want to hear
a word about us.

62
00:12:27,461 --> 00:12:30,034
Done.
We've had that conversation.

63
00:12:34,176 --> 00:12:36,056
You haven't started
on the internal organs yet?

64
00:12:36,261 --> 00:12:38,135
Just a blood sample
for the pericardium.

65
00:12:40,766 --> 00:12:43,886
The maxilla
looks a little deformed.

66
00:12:44,311 --> 00:12:46,683
There's some odd muscle
structure around the canines.

67
00:12:47,105 --> 00:12:49,976
I'm going to start the "Y"
and check the tracheal mucosa.

68
00:12:55,072 --> 00:12:56,614
Let me ask you something.

69
00:12:58,325 --> 00:12:59,523
Honestly...

70
00:13:01,161 --> 00:13:02,721
you ever have
second thoughts about us?

71
00:13:05,749 --> 00:13:06,912
Sometimes.

72
00:13:09,044 --> 00:13:11,202
But then I remember
how much of an asshole you were.

73
00:13:11,630 --> 00:13:12,670
Want to cut me some slack?

74
00:13:12,965 --> 00:13:15,456
You asked for time off,
I gave you time off.

75
00:13:16,510 --> 00:13:17,750
- Look, Curtis...
- I'm trying.

76
00:13:17,886 --> 00:13:19,464
It's over.

77
00:13:38,448 --> 00:13:39,729
Call security!

78
00:13:56,675 --> 00:13:58,050
Came back to finish you off.

79
00:13:58,468 --> 00:14:00,508
Get out of my way, you freak!

80
00:14:07,477 --> 00:14:09,102
Freeze!

81
00:14:10,814 --> 00:14:13,601
Motherfucker,
are you out of your damn mind?!

82
00:15:06,703 --> 00:15:08,281
Hey, you! Freeze!

83
00:15:27,182 --> 00:15:28,511
Hold it right there!

84
00:15:44,449 --> 00:15:46,193
My shoulder...

85
00:15:46,618 --> 00:15:48,196
it's dislocated.

86
00:17:37,521 --> 00:17:38,521
Whistler.

87
00:17:50,284 --> 00:17:51,659
Bringing home strays now?

88
00:17:53,954 --> 00:17:55,365
She's been bitten.

89
00:17:59,835 --> 00:18:00,997
Should've killed her, then.

90
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:03,044
Yeah, I know...

91
00:18:05,507 --> 00:18:07,001
but I didn't.

92
00:18:13,807 --> 00:18:15,800
You watch her close.

93
00:18:16,226 --> 00:18:19,013
If she starts to turn,
you finish her off.

94
00:18:23,233 --> 00:18:24,644
Or I will.

95
00:18:32,242 --> 00:18:33,653
She's borderline.

96
00:18:35,287 --> 00:18:38,122
Another hour,
she'd be well into the change.

97
00:18:40,792 --> 00:18:43,497
Dr. Karen Jenson, listen close.

98
00:18:44,630 --> 00:18:46,622
I'm going to inject you
with allium sativum...

99
00:18:47,049 --> 00:18:48,543
garlic.

100
00:18:48,967 --> 00:18:50,759
This is going to hurt... a lot.

101
00:18:51,178 --> 00:18:52,376
It was Quinn.

102
00:18:53,597 --> 00:18:55,139
Frost's little errand boy?

103
00:18:56,433 --> 00:18:58,011
You get a lead on him?

104
00:19:00,270 --> 00:19:01,729
Too bad.

105
00:19:04,441 --> 00:19:05,472
Hold her.

106
00:19:16,787 --> 00:19:18,411
I give her fifty-fifty...

107
00:19:18,830 --> 00:19:21,119
if she makes it
through the night.

108
00:19:47,484 --> 00:19:48,978
Blade...

109
00:19:49,403 --> 00:19:51,111
the Daywalker...

110
00:19:51,530 --> 00:19:53,772
still pursuing
his ridiculous crusade.

111
00:19:57,578 --> 00:19:58,953
How many died?

112
00:20:00,247 --> 00:20:01,990
We don't have an exact count.

113
00:20:02,416 --> 00:20:04,325
Apparently,
he used a lot of silver.

114
00:20:04,751 --> 00:20:08,334
- We're having difficulty...
- Send in Frost.

115
00:20:16,555 --> 00:20:17,717
Deacon Frost.

116
00:20:21,768 --> 00:20:23,311
You can come in now.

117
00:20:58,096 --> 00:20:59,646
These nightclubs of yours
are dangerous.

118
00:20:59,746 --> 00:21:01,140
Are they?

119
00:21:01,558 --> 00:21:04,014
They draw needless attention
to our kind.

120
00:21:04,436 --> 00:21:05,436
You know our policy.

121
00:21:05,687 --> 00:21:07,479
Your policy, not mine.

122
00:21:07,898 --> 00:21:10,056
Our livelihood...

123
00:21:11,276 --> 00:21:14,277
depends on our ability
to blend in...

124
00:21:15,322 --> 00:21:16,697
and our discretion.

125
00:21:17,783 --> 00:21:20,072
Maybe it's time
we forgot about discretion.

126
00:21:21,578 --> 00:21:23,072
We should be ruling
the humans...

127
00:21:23,497 --> 00:21:26,070
not running around making
back-alley treaties with them.

128
00:21:26,500 --> 00:21:28,220
For fuck's sake,
these people are our food...

129
00:21:28,460 --> 00:21:29,705
not our allies.

130
00:21:30,128 --> 00:21:32,999
- You're out of line.
- Am I?

131
00:21:33,423 --> 00:21:35,257
Or maybe I'm just
the first to say out loud...

132
00:21:35,357 --> 00:21:36,505
what we’ve all been thinking.

133
00:21:36,927 --> 00:21:38,338
We have existed this way...

134
00:21:38,762 --> 00:21:41,170
for thousands of years.

135
00:21:41,598 --> 00:21:45,976
Who are you
to challenge our ways?

136
00:21:46,395 --> 00:21:48,637
You're not even a pureblood.

137
00:21:52,067 --> 00:21:53,347
Like it matters.

138
00:21:54,653 --> 00:21:58,104
I was born a vampire...

139
00:21:58,532 --> 00:22:01,865
as was every other member
of this house...

140
00:22:02,286 --> 00:22:03,531
but, you, Frost...

141
00:22:06,915 --> 00:22:09,489
you were merely turned.

142
00:22:11,628 --> 00:22:15,246
The world belongs to us...
not the humans.

143
00:22:16,049 --> 00:22:17,460
You know that.

144
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:24,553
Do we have
any other business to discuss?

145
00:22:24,975 --> 00:22:30,182
There's the matter
of our offshore accounts.

146
00:22:30,606 --> 00:22:33,013
And have you made
the transfer to the...

147
00:22:33,442 --> 00:22:36,443
Gitano, you may wake up one day
and find yourself extinct.

148
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:11,931
You're a week early.

149
00:23:20,822 --> 00:23:23,492
Whistler says I'm building up
a resistance to the serum.

150
00:23:26,912 --> 00:23:29,237
I figured that might happen.

151
00:23:38,465 --> 00:23:40,007
You take care, all right?

152
00:25:25,239 --> 00:25:27,065
I must be getting soft
in my old age...

153
00:25:27,491 --> 00:25:29,733
letting you bring home
a stray like that.

154
00:25:31,036 --> 00:25:33,194
It was damn stupid of you.

155
00:25:33,622 --> 00:25:35,661
Might've lucked out, though.

156
00:25:36,917 --> 00:25:39,325
I checked her background.

157
00:25:42,089 --> 00:25:44,496
It turns out
she's a haematologist.

158
00:25:46,093 --> 00:25:47,966
She might be useful to us.

159
00:25:49,555 --> 00:25:50,965
I doubt it.

160
00:25:52,349 --> 00:25:54,057
I'm serious.

161
00:25:54,476 --> 00:25:56,036
I took a look
at that notebook of hers.

162
00:25:56,353 --> 00:25:58,511
She's onto something.

163
00:26:01,108 --> 00:26:02,732
I had to increase the dose.

164
00:26:04,194 --> 00:26:05,902
It's over 50 milligrams now.

165
00:26:06,321 --> 00:26:07,484
That's getting dangerous.

166
00:26:07,906 --> 00:26:11,489
Just do it... old man.

167
00:27:11,470 --> 00:27:13,795
Wander off the beaten path,
Doctor?

168
00:27:15,682 --> 00:27:17,011
Who are you people?

169
00:27:17,434 --> 00:27:19,012
My name's Abraham Whistler.

170
00:27:20,312 --> 00:27:21,771
You've met Blade.

171
00:27:37,871 --> 00:27:39,828
So, am I a prisoner here?

172
00:27:41,416 --> 00:27:42,959
Not at all.

173
00:27:43,377 --> 00:27:45,029
We just had to take
certain precautions...

174
00:27:45,129 --> 00:27:47,085
before we let you go.

175
00:27:47,506 --> 00:27:50,626
You got to understand,
they're everywhere.

176
00:27:51,051 --> 00:27:52,878
Vampires...

177
00:27:53,303 --> 00:27:54,797
the hominus nocturna.

178
00:27:56,139 --> 00:27:59,057
We hunt them... moving
from one city to the next...

179
00:27:59,476 --> 00:28:00,970
tracking their migrations.

180
00:28:01,395 --> 00:28:04,514
They're hard to kill.
Tend to regenerate.

181
00:28:04,940 --> 00:28:06,420
And I'm supposed
to believe all this?

182
00:28:06,567 --> 00:28:09,437
You already met Mr. Crispy
at the hospital.

183
00:28:09,862 --> 00:28:11,439
What do you think?

184
00:28:13,365 --> 00:28:15,025
So, what do you use, then?

185
00:28:15,450 --> 00:28:16,993
Stakes? Crosses?

186
00:28:17,411 --> 00:28:19,119
Crosses don't do squat.

187
00:28:19,538 --> 00:28:21,863
Some of the legends
are true, though.

188
00:28:22,291 --> 00:28:25,494
Vampires are severely allergic
to silver.

189
00:28:25,919 --> 00:28:29,039
Feed them garlic and they go
into anaphylactic shock.

190
00:28:29,464 --> 00:28:31,184
Then, of course,
there's always sunlight...

191
00:28:31,425 --> 00:28:32,883
ultraviolet rays.

192
00:28:33,302 --> 00:28:35,508
I got this sucker running.

193
00:28:35,929 --> 00:28:37,673
You want to give it a try
tonight?

194
00:28:44,563 --> 00:28:45,678
It's still heavy.

195
00:28:47,274 --> 00:28:48,472
But you're so big.

196
00:28:51,195 --> 00:28:52,755
If you want to live
to see another day...

197
00:28:52,855 --> 00:28:54,174
you'll be out of town
by nightfall.

198
00:28:54,573 --> 00:28:56,566
Where am I supposed to go?

199
00:29:00,412 --> 00:29:02,701
You've been exposed to them.

200
00:29:03,123 --> 00:29:05,910
One way or another, somebody's
going to take you out.

201
00:29:10,797 --> 00:29:12,755
There's a war going on
out there.

202
00:29:14,092 --> 00:29:16,500
Blade, myself, a few others...

203
00:29:16,929 --> 00:29:19,716
we've tried to keep it from
spilling over onto the streets.

204
00:29:20,140 --> 00:29:23,474
Sometimes, people like yourself
get caught in the cross fire.

205
00:29:24,853 --> 00:29:27,012
I have blood samples.
I can go to the police.

206
00:29:27,439 --> 00:29:29,930
They own the police.

207
00:29:30,359 --> 00:29:32,079
You have to understand,
they're everywhere.

208
00:29:32,236 --> 00:29:35,236
Chances are you've seen them
yourself and didn't know it...

209
00:29:35,656 --> 00:29:37,529
on the subway or in a bar.

210
00:29:39,618 --> 00:29:42,287
So that's it?

211
00:29:42,704 --> 00:29:45,575
You guys just patch me up
and send me on my way?

212
00:29:49,628 --> 00:29:50,908
Here.

213
00:29:51,338 --> 00:29:52,749
Vampire mace...

214
00:29:54,341 --> 00:29:56,084
silver nitrate,
essence of garlic.

215
00:29:56,510 --> 00:29:58,799
You keep your eyes open.

216
00:29:59,221 --> 00:30:01,130
Be careful.

217
00:30:05,269 --> 00:30:07,427
One other thing...

218
00:30:07,854 --> 00:30:09,812
buy yourself a gun.

219
00:30:11,275 --> 00:30:13,314
If you start getting
sensitive to daylight...

220
00:30:14,611 --> 00:30:16,403
If you find you're thirsty...

221
00:30:16,822 --> 00:30:19,692
regardless of how much
you had to drink...

222
00:30:20,117 --> 00:30:23,367
then I suggest you take that gun
and use it on yourself.

223
00:30:27,040 --> 00:30:29,448
Better that
than the alternative.

224
00:31:27,351 --> 00:31:29,308
You have been warned before.

225
00:31:29,728 --> 00:31:33,311
These archives are restricted
to the members of the House.

226
00:31:36,276 --> 00:31:37,901
You are wasting your time.

227
00:31:38,320 --> 00:31:39,980
It's a dead language.

228
00:31:40,405 --> 00:31:42,979
The ancient texts
can never be translated.

229
00:31:45,369 --> 00:31:47,445
You wouldn't even
understand them.

230
00:31:49,790 --> 00:31:52,115
Damn it, Frost!
I'm talking to you!

231
00:31:56,421 --> 00:31:58,213
Keep your voice down, Gitano.

232
00:32:00,717 --> 00:32:01,717
We're in a library.

233
00:32:02,135 --> 00:32:03,250
You don't need to shout.

234
00:32:04,805 --> 00:32:06,299
What are you up to?

235
00:32:18,485 --> 00:32:20,525
What are you going to do?

236
00:32:25,951 --> 00:32:27,149
What?

237
00:32:32,541 --> 00:32:34,083
You bore me.

238
00:33:09,077 --> 00:33:10,785
Rememberer what we told you.

239
00:33:11,997 --> 00:33:13,408
You keep your eyes open.

240
00:33:13,832 --> 00:33:15,326
They're everywhere.

241
00:33:17,169 --> 00:33:18,793
But it's daytime!

242
00:34:18,522 --> 00:34:19,850
How you doing?

243
00:35:38,310 --> 00:35:40,018
Hi, there.

244
00:35:40,437 --> 00:35:43,010
I'm sorry. Whoa! Hold on.

245
00:35:43,440 --> 00:35:45,183
Police officer. I'm sorry, OK?

246
00:35:45,609 --> 00:35:48,064
I didn't mean to scare you.
The front door was open.

247
00:35:48,487 --> 00:35:49,458
What are you doing here?

248
00:35:49,558 --> 00:35:52,400
I'm here on a routine check.

249
00:35:52,824 --> 00:35:55,576
Look, I'm Officer Krieger,
42nd precinct.

250
00:35:55,994 --> 00:35:58,865
You're Karen Jenson, right?

251
00:36:00,707 --> 00:36:02,067
Your co-workers
at the hospital...

252
00:36:02,376 --> 00:36:04,534
said that you were kidnapped
last night.

253
00:36:06,088 --> 00:36:07,088
Are you OK?

254
00:36:07,506 --> 00:36:10,756
What happened
to the other doctor I was with?

255
00:36:12,469 --> 00:36:15,174
Curtis Webb? He died.

256
00:36:16,557 --> 00:36:19,178
Don’t worry about that
right now, OK?

257
00:36:20,143 --> 00:36:21,554
Why?

258
00:36:21,979 --> 00:36:24,434
Because you're dead, too, bitch.

259
00:36:27,776 --> 00:36:29,603
Bitch! What is it?

260
00:36:32,489 --> 00:36:33,489
What is this, garlic?

261
00:36:33,740 --> 00:36:35,982
He said it would work
against vampires.

262
00:36:36,410 --> 00:36:37,904
Vampires?

263
00:36:38,996 --> 00:36:41,202
Who said I was a vampire?

264
00:36:43,584 --> 00:36:44,615
Nobody.

265
00:36:49,548 --> 00:36:51,291
He's a familiar...

266
00:36:52,175 --> 00:36:53,835
a vampire wannabe.

267
00:36:55,137 --> 00:36:57,260
If he's loyal enough...

268
00:36:57,681 --> 00:37:00,433
and he proves himself,
maybe his master will turn him.

269
00:37:02,603 --> 00:37:04,642
Wait a minute.
You used me as bait?

270
00:37:05,063 --> 00:37:06,688
Get over it.

271
00:37:11,570 --> 00:37:12,570
