527
01:00:36,225 --> 01:00:37,802
He told me what you are.

528
01:00:41,521 --> 01:00:43,313
You don't know me.

529
01:00:43,732 --> 01:00:45,689
You don't know
anything about me.

530
01:00:48,987 --> 01:00:51,063
I'm not human.

531
01:00:53,867 --> 01:00:55,065
You look human to me...

532
01:00:55,494 --> 01:00:57,985
Humans don't drink blood.

533
01:00:58,413 --> 01:01:00,453
That was a long time ago.

534
01:01:02,125 --> 01:01:03,952
Maybe you should let that go.

535
01:01:06,838 --> 01:01:08,381
I have spent my whole life...

536
01:01:08,799 --> 01:01:10,957
looking for that thing
that killed my mother.

537
01:01:12,553 --> 01:01:14,545
It made me what I am.

538
01:01:18,016 --> 01:01:21,017
And every time I take
one of those monsters out...

539
01:01:21,436 --> 01:01:23,974
I get a little piece
of that life back...

540
01:01:24,398 --> 01:01:27,102
so don't you tell me
about forgetting.

541
01:01:31,154 --> 01:01:33,112
He took us by surprise!

542
01:01:33,407 --> 01:01:35,287
Two of them against
your entire security force?

543
01:01:35,742 --> 01:01:37,902
Don't put that shit on me,
'cause you were there, too!

544
01:01:38,120 --> 01:01:39,480
I'm sure Deacon will
appreciate...

545
01:01:39,913 --> 01:01:42,665
...stabbed in the balls for it!
You little skeez!

546
01:01:43,083 --> 01:01:44,705
Don't see the lifestyle
really suits you.

547
01:01:44,805 --> 01:01:47,067
I'll put this stump through
that shit-eating grin of yours.

548
01:01:47,167 --> 01:01:50,497
Face it. You were sloppy.
You got what you deserved.

549
01:01:55,053 --> 01:01:57,758
Deac, let me take this guy out.
Look what he fuckin' did!

550
01:01:58,181 --> 01:01:59,181
He took my hand again!

551
01:01:59,391 --> 01:02:02,178
Listen to me. I want him alive.

552
01:02:02,603 --> 01:02:05,010
What the fuck are you talk...
You want him alive?

553
01:02:05,439 --> 01:02:07,559
We've been tryin' to kill
this motherfucker for years.

554
01:02:07,941 --> 01:02:09,483
Are you
out of your fuckin' mind?

555
01:02:11,069 --> 01:02:14,154
Big guy, relax.

556
01:02:14,573 --> 01:02:15,853
Be patient.

557
01:02:17,451 --> 01:02:19,028
Now, we got a lot to do here.

558
01:02:20,037 --> 01:02:21,579
I need you, man.

559
01:02:25,542 --> 01:02:27,416
I need you.

560
01:03:10,879 --> 01:03:12,457
Morning.

561
01:03:12,881 --> 01:03:14,459
How you feelin'?

562
01:03:23,684 --> 01:03:24,882
Look at that.

563
01:03:29,064 --> 01:03:31,935
Gettin' a little toasty
out here, huh?

564
01:03:34,278 --> 01:03:37,812
When's the last time you stopped
to appreciate a good sunrise?

565
01:03:38,240 --> 01:03:40,000
Oh, that's right.
You were born a vampire...

566
01:03:40,158 --> 01:03:42,151
so you never had
the pleasure, have you?

567
01:03:42,578 --> 01:03:44,985
That's OK. It's all right.

568
01:03:45,414 --> 01:03:46,659
Least we’re here together.

569
01:03:47,082 --> 01:03:48,624
Share the moment...

570
01:03:49,042 --> 01:03:51,082
which means a lot to me
by the way, really.

571
01:03:51,503 --> 01:03:52,748
I mean that.

572
01:03:55,215 --> 01:03:57,374
'Cause actually,
when you get to know me...

573
01:03:57,801 --> 01:03:59,794
I'm a fairly
sentimental type of guy.

574
01:04:00,220 --> 01:04:02,343
Bit of an innocent,
you might say.

575
01:04:05,309 --> 01:04:07,218
Do what you want, Frost.

576
01:04:08,312 --> 01:04:10,269
Doesn't make any difference.

577
01:04:11,732 --> 01:04:13,689
You just don't fuckin' get it.

578
01:04:15,819 --> 01:04:17,179
You're never gonna be
a pureblood.

579
01:04:17,529 --> 01:04:18,988
Hold him.

580
01:04:21,533 --> 01:04:23,442
You will never rule us!

581
01:04:36,340 --> 01:04:38,000
Jesus Christ.

582
01:04:38,425 --> 01:04:39,588
Have a nice day.

583
01:04:40,427 --> 01:04:41,427
Sorry, you old dog.

584
01:04:41,762 --> 01:04:43,522
You just got a little too long
in the tooth.

585
01:04:45,224 --> 01:04:47,133
What, man? That was funny.

586
01:04:47,559 --> 01:04:48,840
"Long, tooth." Funny.

587
01:04:49,269 --> 01:04:51,677
Did I tell you the one about...

588
01:05:21,385 --> 01:05:23,377
What have you done
with Dragonetti?

589
01:05:30,477 --> 01:05:32,766
Let's get down to business,
shall we?

590
01:05:33,188 --> 01:05:35,347
I need 12 volunteers.

591
01:05:46,827 --> 01:05:48,238
What is this?

592
01:05:50,038 --> 01:05:51,912
Smells like a vampire
wiped his ass with it.

593
01:05:52,332 --> 01:05:53,613
I took it from the archives.

594
01:05:54,042 --> 01:05:55,122
It's written in blood.

595
01:05:55,544 --> 01:05:57,786
It's from The Book of Erebus.

596
01:06:03,635 --> 01:06:05,347
I think it's what Frost
has been workin' on.

597
01:06:05,447 --> 01:06:07,130
It's somethin' about
the Blood God...

598
01:06:07,556 --> 01:06:08,884
the Spirits of the Twelve.

599
01:06:09,308 --> 01:06:11,431
I don't know.
I can't make out the rest of it.

600
01:06:11,852 --> 01:06:13,429
Maybe this'll help.

601
01:06:14,438 --> 01:06:15,849
I’ll figure out something.

602
01:06:17,482 --> 01:06:18,763
So what's all this?

603
01:06:19,193 --> 01:06:21,399
Took a trip
to the hospital last night...

604
01:06:21,820 --> 01:06:23,398
borrowed some equipment.

605
01:06:23,822 --> 01:06:25,779
For your miracle cure?

606
01:06:28,368 --> 01:06:29,368
This is E.D.T.A.

607
01:06:29,703 --> 01:06:30,703
It's an anticoagulant.

608
01:06:30,913 --> 01:06:33,285
We use it to treat blood clots.

609
01:06:34,458 --> 01:06:36,139
Now look what happens
when I introduce it...

610
01:06:36,239 --> 01:06:37,958
onto a sample of vampire blood.

611
01:06:40,422 --> 01:06:41,964
Take a step back.

612
01:06:42,382 --> 01:06:44,007
The reaction's energetic.

613
01:06:53,352 --> 01:06:54,352
Some cure.

614
01:06:54,519 --> 01:06:57,189
I didn't say E.D.T.A.
Was a cure.

615
01:06:57,606 --> 01:07:01,686
But maybe you could use it
to explode some vampire heads.

616
01:07:04,196 --> 01:07:06,983
Wait a minute.
I need a sample of your blood.

617
01:07:07,407 --> 01:07:08,407
Later.

618
01:07:08,617 --> 01:07:10,444
Gotta go downtown.

619
01:07:10,869 --> 01:07:11,869
Need some serum.

620
01:07:12,162 --> 01:07:13,162
Serum can wait.

621
01:07:13,539 --> 01:07:15,116
This is important.

622
01:07:37,187 --> 01:07:38,468
Is he sick?

623
01:07:38,897 --> 01:07:40,095
Cancer.

624
01:07:42,693 --> 01:07:44,436
You have a lot of love for him,
don't you?

625
01:07:45,821 --> 01:07:47,481
We have a good arrangement.

626
01:07:47,906 --> 01:07:50,658
He makes the weapons.
I use 'em.

627
01:07:54,496 --> 01:07:56,323
My mother used to say...

628
01:07:56,748 --> 01:07:59,074
"a cold heart is a dead heart."

629
01:08:16,643 --> 01:08:18,387
You don't look so good.

630
01:08:19,688 --> 01:08:20,688
I'm just a little tired.

631
01:08:20,856 --> 01:08:22,683
You know we've been...

632
01:08:23,108 --> 01:08:24,483
workin' all night.

633
01:08:27,446 --> 01:08:29,569
I guess we didn't catch it
in time.

634
01:08:31,158 --> 01:08:35,156
You got another day...
two at the most.

635
01:08:39,458 --> 01:08:41,201
For what it's worth, I'm sorry.

636
01:08:41,627 --> 01:08:44,830
You make it sound like
I'm already dead.

637
01:09:29,341 --> 01:09:31,049
How you doin', chief?

638
01:09:32,386 --> 01:09:33,417
Easy.

639
01:09:35,055 --> 01:09:36,535
Wouldn’t want
our little friend here...

640
01:09:36,635 --> 01:09:39,184
to wind up on the back
of a milk carton, would we?

641
01:09:42,354 --> 01:09:44,560
It's nice to finally meet you.

642
01:09:44,982 --> 01:09:46,974
Had my eye on you for years.

643
01:09:47,401 --> 01:09:48,515
I know all about you...

644
01:09:48,944 --> 01:09:51,517
your serum, Whistler...
everything.

645
01:09:51,947 --> 01:09:53,774
Sunblock.

646
01:09:54,199 --> 01:09:55,907
Hey, it's a start, right?

647
01:09:56,326 --> 01:09:58,782
The goal, of course,
is to be like you...

648
01:09:59,204 --> 01:10:00,367
the Daywalker.

649
01:10:01,957 --> 01:10:03,996
You got the best of both worlds,
don't you?

650
01:10:05,043 --> 01:10:07,665
All our strengths...
none of our weaknesses.

651
01:10:08,088 --> 01:10:10,793
Maybe I don't see it that way.

652
01:10:11,216 --> 01:10:13,886
Oh, so it's back to pretending
we're human again?

653
01:10:14,303 --> 01:10:17,672
Come on. Spare me
the Uncle Tom routine, OK?

654
01:10:18,098 --> 01:10:20,885
You can't keep denying
what you are, man.

655
01:10:21,310 --> 01:10:24,264
You think the humans will ever
accept a half-breed like you?

656
01:10:24,688 --> 01:10:27,144
They can't.
They're afraid of you.

657
01:10:28,650 --> 01:10:29,931
And they should be.

658
01:10:30,360 --> 01:10:31,331
You're an animal.

659
01:10:31,431 --> 01:10:33,443
You're a fuckin' maniac.

660
01:10:36,533 --> 01:10:37,533
Look at 'em.

661
01:10:37,951 --> 01:10:39,908
They're cattle...

662
01:10:40,329 --> 01:10:41,906
pieces of meat.

663
01:10:42,331 --> 01:10:45,000
What difference does it make
how their world ends?

664
01:10:45,417 --> 01:10:49,118
Plague, war, famine.

665
01:10:49,546 --> 01:10:51,918
Morality
doesn't even enter into it.

666
01:10:53,050 --> 01:10:54,995
We're just a function
of natural selection, man...

667
01:10:55,095 --> 01:10:57,091
the new race.

668
01:10:58,597 --> 01:11:01,218
Looks like
your mascara's running.

669
01:11:08,398 --> 01:11:10,272
I'm offering you a truce.

670
01:11:10,692 --> 01:11:11,973
I want you with us.

671
01:11:12,402 --> 01:11:14,395
What do you think, I'm stupid?

672
01:11:22,996 --> 01:11:24,953
You're familiar
with the Blood God.

673
01:11:27,793 --> 01:11:29,999
You're nothing to me...

674
01:11:30,420 --> 01:11:32,994
but another dead vampire.

675
01:11:33,423 --> 01:11:35,961
You're an idiot. You know that?

676
01:11:36,385 --> 01:11:38,305
I came down here
offering you an easy way out...

677
01:11:38,637 --> 01:11:40,962
and you spit it right back
in my fuckin' face.

678
01:11:42,683 --> 01:11:44,509
Careful.

679
01:11:47,646 --> 01:11:50,137
What do I care?

680
01:11:50,566 --> 01:11:52,523
They're nothing but cattle...

681
01:11:52,943 --> 01:11:54,437
just like you said.

682
01:11:54,862 --> 01:11:58,230
If you wanna take the hard road,
be my guest...

683
01:11:58,657 --> 01:12:00,497
but I promise you,
by the time this is over...

684
01:12:00,826 --> 01:12:03,151
you're gonna wish they never
cut you from your mother's...

685
01:12:38,697 --> 01:12:39,942
Go home.

686
01:12:43,785 --> 01:12:44,715
It was simple.

687
01:12:44,815 --> 01:12:46,488
Why do vampires need
to drink blood?

688
01:12:46,914 --> 01:12:48,874
'Cause their own blood
can't sustain haemoglobin.

689
01:12:49,291 --> 01:12:51,912
It's a genetic defect,
just like haemolytic anaemia.

690
01:12:52,336 --> 01:12:54,743
That means that we have
to treat it with gene therapy...

691
01:12:55,172 --> 01:12:58,173
rewrite the victim's DNA
with a retrovirus.

692
01:12:58,592 --> 01:13:00,964
They've been using it
on sickle cell anaemia.

693
01:13:01,386 --> 01:13:02,549
Are you sure that's safe?

694
01:13:02,971 --> 01:13:06,056
I have no idea,
but I don't have a choice, do I?

695
01:13:08,477 --> 01:13:10,434
You actually think
this could work?

696
01:13:10,854 --> 01:13:13,891
On me... yes.

697
01:13:15,025 --> 01:13:16,733
On Blade, I'm not so sure.

698
01:13:17,152 --> 01:13:20,319
He didn't contract vampirism
from a bite like I did.

699
01:13:20,739 --> 01:13:21,937
He was born with it.

700
01:13:22,366 --> 01:13:24,074
It's part of his DNA.

701
01:13:24,493 --> 01:13:27,031
I'm sure I can cure
his thirst...

702
01:13:27,454 --> 01:13:28,652
but it's gonna take time.

703
01:13:29,081 --> 01:13:31,120
We're out of time.

704
01:13:31,542 --> 01:13:33,451
You saw what was on that disk.

705
01:13:38,590 --> 01:13:40,084
Damn.

706
01:13:42,094 --> 01:13:43,292
Get out of here.

707
01:14:07,995 --> 01:14:10,320
I said get out of here!

708
01:14:16,420 --> 01:14:19,705
Nice place.
Took us a while to find it!

709
01:14:27,931 --> 01:14:29,051
Bite me and get it over with.

710
01:14:29,391 --> 01:14:30,802
I ain't gonna bite you.

711
01:14:44,281 --> 01:14:45,479
Do your thing.

712
01:16:06,530 --> 01:16:08,985
Frost took her.

713
01:16:16,665 --> 01:16:18,124
Listen to me.

714
01:16:21,169 --> 01:16:22,368
The disk.

715
01:16:23,672 --> 01:16:24,870
He decoded it.

716
01:16:25,299 --> 01:16:28,134
Frost is trying to...

717
01:16:28,552 --> 01:16:32,051
trigger
a fuckin' vampire apocalypse.

718
01:16:34,182 --> 01:16:36,175
There's some kind of...

719
01:16:36,602 --> 01:16:39,768
vampire god
he's trying to resurrect.

720
01:16:41,356 --> 01:16:42,934
La Magra.

721
01:16:46,320 --> 01:16:48,063
You're the key.

722
01:16:49,531 --> 01:16:51,323
He needs your blood...

723
01:16:55,037 --> 01:16:57,195
the blood of the Daywalker.

724
01:16:59,791 --> 01:17:02,496
You're the chosen one.

725
01:17:06,048 --> 01:17:07,328
Listen to me, Blade.

726
01:17:08,842 --> 01:17:10,420
You can't go after him.

727
01:17:10,844 --> 01:17:12,125
Bullshit.

728
01:17:12,554 --> 01:17:14,463
If Frost gets his hands
on you...

729
01:17:14,890 --> 01:17:17,297
it's all over.

730
01:17:20,270 --> 01:17:22,393
There'll be armies
of the motherfuckers.

731
01:17:25,734 --> 01:17:26,897
Shit.

732
01:17:31,907 --> 01:17:33,449
You're gonna have
to finish me off.

733
01:17:35,285 --> 01:17:36,827
Don’t want me coming back.

734
01:17:38,747 --> 01:17:40,656
We can treat the wounds.

735
01:17:42,334 --> 01:17:43,745
It's too far gone.

736
01:17:44,169 --> 01:17:46,292
You know that.

737
01:17:49,633 --> 01:17:52,302
Give me your gun.

738
01:17:56,431 --> 01:17:59,183
Give me the goddamn gun.

739
01:18:24,251 --> 01:18:25,251
Now walk away...

740
01:18:25,627 --> 01:18:27,953
you stupid son of a bitch.

741
01:18:32,718 --> 01:18:35,173
Walk the fuck away.

742
01:18:56,158 --> 01:18:57,318
By the time you watch this...

743
01:18:57,451 --> 01:18:58,851
your friend Whistler
should be dead.

744
01:18:59,161 --> 01:19:00,655
If it makes any difference
to you...

745
01:19:01,079 --> 01:19:02,408
he put up quite a fight.

746
01:19:02,831 --> 01:19:05,500
You can find us
at the Edgewood Towers.

747
01:20:43,765 --> 01:20:45,888
You seem a bit tense.

748
01:20:46,310 --> 01:20:47,934
A bit pent-up maybe...

749
01:20:48,353 --> 01:20:49,931
like you need
to release something.

750
01:20:51,523 --> 01:20:52,523
You know?

751
01:20:52,733 --> 01:20:53,733
Blade not...

752
01:20:54,902 --> 01:20:56,360
givin' it to you maybe?

753
01:20:56,778 --> 01:20:58,901
I don't know. I just...

754
01:21:00,282 --> 01:21:02,321
I see such a beautiful woman.

755
01:21:04,036 --> 01:21:05,316
Great skin.

756
01:21:08,040 --> 01:21:09,783
I'd like to see you happy,
that's all.

757
01:21:10,209 --> 01:21:13,412
Is this the part
where you offer to turn me?

758
01:21:15,005 --> 01:21:17,081
It's either that or a body bag.

759
01:21:17,507 --> 01:21:20,378
Go ahead. Bite me.

760
01:21:20,802 --> 01:21:23,424
I'll just cure myself.

761
01:21:23,847 --> 01:21:26,599
I did it before,
and I can do it again.

762
01:21:27,017 --> 01:21:28,476
There is no cure, baby.

763
01:21:28,894 --> 01:21:31,136
There is
if you've been bitten...

764
01:21:31,563 --> 01:21:33,770
if you were once human.

765
01:21:39,112 --> 01:21:41,686
How'd you get that scar, Deacon?

766
01:21:42,115 --> 01:21:44,571
A born vampire has the power
to regenerate from birth.

767
01:21:44,993 --> 01:21:47,864
You must've gotten scarred
before you were turned.

768
01:21:48,288 --> 01:21:50,447
Isn't that right?

769
01:21:50,874 --> 01:21:52,701
Vampires like you
aren't a species.

770
01:21:53,126 --> 01:21:54,953
You're just infected...

771
01:21:55,379 --> 01:21:58,000
a virus,
a sexually transmitted disease.

772
01:21:58,423 --> 01:21:59,743
I'll tell you what we are,
sister.

773
01:21:59,883 --> 01:22:02,090
We're the top
of the fuckin' food chain.

774
01:22:02,511 --> 01:22:04,231
The Blood God's coming,
and after tonight...

775
01:22:04,638 --> 01:22:06,298
you people are fuckin' history.

776
01:22:07,766 --> 01:22:08,929
He's a hurricane...

777
01:22:09,351 --> 01:22:11,059
an act of God.

778
01:22:11,478 --> 01:22:14,396
Anyone caught in his path
will instantly be turned.

779
01:22:16,316 --> 01:22:17,645
Everyone you've ever known...

780
01:22:18,068 --> 01:22:20,855
everyone
you've ever fucking loved.

781
01:22:21,280 --> 01:22:24,565
It won’t matter
who's pureblood and who's not.

782
01:22:24,992 --> 01:22:27,696
How are you gonna cure
the whole fuckin' world?

783
01:22:34,418 --> 01:22:36,541
And Blade's blood is the key.

784
01:22:36,962 --> 01:22:38,586
We got an intruder.

785
01:23:07,951 --> 01:23:10,151
I don't think you understand.
This dude is fuckin' bad.

786
01:23:10,287 --> 01:23:11,995
He had 20 guys around him...

787
01:23:12,414 --> 01:23:13,894
and he's got shit
he throws at you...

788
01:23:14,291 --> 01:23:15,489
Yeah, the swords.

789
01:23:15,918 --> 01:23:17,467
Throw it in the air,
catch it underneath.

790
01:23:17,567 --> 01:23:18,574
Yeah. Shut the fuck up!

791
01:23:19,004 --> 01:23:20,323
There's no intruder
where we are.

792
01:23:20,423 --> 01:23:21,881
Look, make it happen, all right?

793
01:23:22,299 --> 01:23:23,544
It's one guy on foot.

794
01:23:28,263 --> 01:23:29,923
That's him! Get him!

795
01:23:49,952 --> 01:23:50,983
Why am I hearing gunfire?

796
01:23:51,411 --> 01:23:53,737
Did I tell anybody
to start shooting?

797
01:23:54,164 --> 01:23:55,623
I need him alive.

798
01:24:00,087 --> 01:24:01,332
Please!

799
01:24:01,755 --> 01:24:03,000
I just work for them!

800
01:24:05,300 --> 01:24:06,700
Jesus Christ.
Lock this place down.

801
01:24:07,094 --> 01:24:08,292
Yes, sir!

802
01:25:55,577 --> 01:25:57,285
Eric?

803
01:26:08,298 --> 01:26:10,006
But you died.

804
01:26:11,301 --> 01:26:13,377
I came back, Eric.

805
01:26:13,804 --> 01:26:15,132
That very same night...

806
01:26:16,890 --> 01:26:19,512
when Deacon welcomed me
into his arms.

807
01:26:36,493 --> 01:26:38,486
Jesus Christ.
I thought you'd be happy.

808
01:26:40,455 --> 01:26:42,335
You're finally reunited,
and you act like this?

809
01:26:43,917 --> 01:26:45,874
Blade, give it up. It's over.

810
01:26:46,295 --> 01:26:48,536
She belongs to me, buddy.

811
01:26:51,425 --> 01:26:52,587
Don't look so surprised.

812
01:26:53,010 --> 01:26:54,504
You spent your whole life...

813
01:26:54,928 --> 01:26:57,336
looking for the vampire
who bit your mother.

814
01:26:57,764 --> 01:26:59,722
Well, here I am.

815
01:27:02,603 --> 01:27:05,473
Who would ever guess you'd
survive your mother's death?

816
01:27:05,898 --> 01:27:06,898
But you did.

817
01:27:07,274 --> 01:27:08,519
And here we are...

818
01:27:08,942 --> 01:27:11,267
one big happy fuckin' family.

819
01:27:22,664 --> 01:27:24,456
I need my serum.

820
01:27:27,169 --> 01:27:30,372
Maybe when we get outta this,
I'll take your miracle cure.

821
01:27:30,797 --> 01:27:32,375
There's one catch.

822
01:27:36,303 --> 01:27:37,927
If it works...

823
01:27:38,347 --> 01:27:40,802
you'll lose your strength...

824
01:27:41,225 --> 01:27:43,016
and your ability to regenerate.

825
01:27:44,144 --> 01:27:46,184
You'll be completely human.

826
01:28:50,878 --> 01:28:52,420
Glad you could make it.

827
01:28:52,838 --> 01:28:55,163
Thanks for the shades.

828
01:28:57,467 --> 01:28:59,045
Our ancestors
called this place...

829
01:28:59,469 --> 01:29:01,261
the Temple of Eternal Night.

830
01:29:04,349 --> 01:29:05,844
Nice, isn't it?

831
01:29:06,268 --> 01:29:08,841
Apparently, these geniuses
forgot it ever existed.

832
01:29:09,271 --> 01:29:11,643
Fortunately for us...

833
01:29:12,065 --> 01:29:16,359
I'm what you might call
a student of history.

834
01:29:29,958 --> 01:29:31,203
Why are we here?

835
01:29:33,712 --> 01:29:37,247
This temple was built
for one glorious moment...

836
01:29:37,674 --> 01:29:40,924
this night, for the Blood God.

837
01:29:49,228 --> 01:29:50,473
Thanks.

838
01:29:55,692 --> 01:29:57,270
Let's see this sword of yours.

839
01:30:00,781 --> 01:30:01,943
Well.

840
01:30:02,366 --> 01:30:03,366
Titanium, right?

841
01:30:03,534 --> 01:30:05,573
Acid-etched?

842
01:30:08,372 --> 01:30:10,115
I'll get used
to a weapon like this.

843
01:30:16,338 --> 01:30:19,754
What? You look surprised.

844
01:30:20,801 --> 01:30:23,090
I told you, Blade,
I know everything about you.

845
01:30:24,972 --> 01:30:25,972
Hold out your arm, Quinn.

846
01:30:26,223 --> 01:30:28,050
Why, man?
They're, like, all better.

847
01:30:28,475 --> 01:30:30,931
Hold out your arm. Now.

848
01:30:34,690 --> 01:30:35,888
Deac, l...

849
01:30:41,113 --> 01:30:42,311
Just kidding.

850
01:30:45,200 --> 01:30:48,154
He was fuckin' with me.

851
01:30:51,665 --> 01:30:54,417
He can't hear you, honey.
The thirst has got him now.

852
01:31:01,133 --> 01:31:02,133
What do we have here?

853
01:31:02,509 --> 01:31:05,214
The precious serum.

854
01:31:07,431 --> 01:31:08,911
How long's it been
since you shot up?

855
01:31:09,057 --> 01:31:11,465
Twelve, thirteen hours maybe?

856
01:31:11,894 --> 01:31:15,428
I bet you're just dying
for a drink, aren't you?

857
01:31:17,900 --> 01:31:19,098
What's it feel like?

858
01:31:21,028 --> 01:31:22,652
Is your blood on fire?

859
01:31:23,071 --> 01:31:25,147
Try some.

860
01:31:25,574 --> 01:31:27,863
You might like it.

861
01:31:28,285 --> 01:31:30,361
Thanks, but I prefer
the real thing.

862
01:31:31,079 --> 01:31:32,989
In any event...

863
01:31:33,123 --> 01:31:35,282
I don't think you'll be
needing these anymore.

864
01:31:42,841 --> 01:31:44,039
It's a shame, you know?

865
01:31:45,302 --> 01:31:46,782
When I think
of what you've become...

866
01:31:47,095 --> 01:31:49,384
what you should have become.

867
01:31:49,806 --> 01:31:51,431
I guess I don't blame you.

868
01:31:51,850 --> 01:31:53,530
I mean, with everything
that's happened...

869
01:31:53,644 --> 01:31:56,479
it's the human side of you
that's made you weak.

870
01:31:56,897 --> 01:31:58,377
You should've listened
to your blood.

871
01:31:58,690 --> 01:32:00,482
Say what you want...

872
01:32:00,901 --> 01:32:04,151
but, I promise you,
you'll be dead by dawn.

873
01:32:08,700 --> 01:32:09,981
Get him outta here.

874
01:32:14,331 --> 01:32:16,371
Get these fucks downstairs.
Now.

875
01:32:16,792 --> 01:32:18,619
Come on. Let's go.

876
01:32:25,092 --> 01:32:27,499
Don’t worry, sweetheart.
We haven’t forgotten about you.

877
01:32:27,928 --> 01:32:28,928
Oh, no, baby.

878
01:32:29,096 --> 01:32:31,338
We got something real special
planned for you.

879
01:32:32,724 --> 01:32:35,262
That surfer boy had a nice ass.
I sucked him dry.

880
01:32:35,686 --> 01:32:37,096
And you’d figure he'd turn, man.

881
01:32:37,521 --> 01:32:38,830
Yeah, but he didn't turn,
did he?

882
01:32:38,930 --> 01:32:40,338
No. He turned into
some kinda zombie.

883
01:32:40,438 --> 01:32:42,313
It happens sometimes, cutie.

884
01:32:43,735 --> 01:32:45,146
He was fuckin' tripped out.

885
01:32:46,154 --> 01:32:47,154
Pathetic.

886
01:32:47,364 --> 01:32:49,484
These guys are complete scum.
They'll eat anything...

887
01:32:49,783 --> 01:32:53,484
animals, rodents, corpses,
and sometimes...

888
01:32:54,872 --> 01:32:56,070
they'll even eat vampires.

889
01:32:56,498 --> 01:32:57,498
That's a plus.

890
01:32:57,916 --> 01:32:59,156
And bearing that all in mind...

891
01:32:59,376 --> 01:33:01,250
I'd like you to meet
an old friend of yours.

892
01:33:07,384 --> 01:33:08,582
It's too bad.

893
01:33:09,011 --> 01:33:10,920
I kinda liked her.

894
01:33:11,346 --> 01:33:12,544
What a waste.

895
01:33:34,244 --> 01:33:36,201
I don't know
what's happening to me.

896
01:33:37,372 --> 01:33:38,867
No pulse.

897
01:33:39,291 --> 01:33:42,577
And, of course, there's
the question of lividity.

898
01:33:54,723 --> 01:33:56,965
I never thought
I would see you again.

899
01:33:57,392 --> 01:33:58,935
Tell me, Karen...

900
01:33:59,353 --> 01:34:01,392
do you ever have second thoughts
about us?

901
01:35:37,534 --> 01:35:39,194
Poor child.

902
01:35:40,954 --> 01:35:42,532
You're so sick.

903
01:35:43,874 --> 01:35:45,913
So thirsty.

904
01:35:46,919 --> 01:35:48,294
Don't touch me.

905
01:35:50,839 --> 01:35:53,413
Eric, look at me.

906
01:35:53,842 --> 01:35:56,167
Vampires are my people now.

907
01:35:56,595 --> 01:35:58,219
I'm one of them.

908
01:35:59,389 --> 01:36:00,718
Can't be.

909
01:36:02,267 --> 01:36:04,011
Yes, it can.

910
01:36:07,189 --> 01:36:08,897
Try to understand, Eric.

911
01:36:10,817 --> 01:36:13,273
Your mother
died a long time ago.

912
01:36:15,656 --> 01:36:17,114
I've hunted...

913
01:36:18,742 --> 01:36:20,236
I've killed...

914
01:36:22,579 --> 01:36:24,406
and I've enjoyed it.

915
01:36:26,083 --> 01:36:27,281
Haven't you?

916
01:36:29,002 --> 01:36:30,461
I know you have.

917
01:36:33,340 --> 01:36:36,376
Sooner or later,
the thirst always wins.

918
01:37:20,888 --> 01:37:22,133
Come on.

919
01:37:28,896 --> 01:37:30,141
Spread them out.

920
01:37:31,273 --> 01:37:33,811
One on each glyph,
under the towers.

921
01:37:34,234 --> 01:37:36,026
Make it perfect.

922
01:38:17,194 --> 01:38:18,392
Bring the elevator up.

923
01:38:58,443 --> 01:38:59,772
You stupid girl.

924
01:39:00,195 --> 01:39:01,562
What do you think
is going to happen?

925
01:39:01,662 --> 01:39:03,528
La Magra? The Blood God?

926
01:39:03,949 --> 01:39:06,985
That's a fairy tale
for pretty little vampires.

927
01:39:07,411 --> 01:39:08,891
Then why are you sweating,
pureblood?

928
01:39:10,330 --> 01:39:12,406
You're afraid
we're gonna steal your soul...

929
01:39:12,833 --> 01:39:14,991
your pureblood spirit?

930
01:39:15,419 --> 01:39:16,996
You should be.

931
01:39:17,421 --> 01:39:18,749
Read the prophecy.

932
01:39:19,172 --> 01:39:22,458
It's time you fucks contributed
something to the cause.

933
01:39:26,680 --> 01:39:28,720
Even if Frost is right...

934
01:39:29,141 --> 01:39:30,849
you really think he cares
about you?

935
01:39:31,268 --> 01:39:34,138
You're gonna die
just like the rest of us.

936
01:40:10,724 --> 01:40:13,096
Tonight, the age of man
comes to an end.

937
01:40:13,518 --> 01:40:15,476
No more compromises.

938
01:40:15,896 --> 01:40:17,355
We're gonna be gods.

939
01:40:18,857 --> 01:40:20,055
Of course we are.

940
01:40:23,445 --> 01:40:24,445
I'm gonna be naughty.

941
01:40:24,863 --> 01:40:27,698
I'm gonna be
a naughty vampire god.

942
01:40:36,375 --> 01:40:37,833
Gotta stop...

943
01:40:39,962 --> 01:40:41,504
Save your strength.

944
01:40:41,922 --> 01:40:43,167
Blue.

945
01:40:45,259 --> 01:40:47,631
You're hypovolaemic.
You're bleeding to death.

946
01:40:48,053 --> 01:40:51,422
Need... serum.

947
01:41:16,290 --> 01:41:17,488
Listen to me.

948
01:41:19,001 --> 01:41:21,408
I want you
to take some of my blood.

949
01:41:29,303 --> 01:41:31,628
Look, just do it.

950
01:41:57,331 --> 01:41:58,576
Is everybody thirsty?

951
01:41:58,999 --> 01:42:02,783
I hope you're all
very fucking thirsty.

952
01:42:23,482 --> 01:42:24,680
Don't stop.

953
01:43:43,687 --> 01:43:45,181
How was it?

954
01:44:58,595 --> 01:45:00,255
I'm your mother.

955
01:45:02,599 --> 01:45:04,722
You wouldn't hurt your mother...

956
01:45:05,143 --> 01:45:06,388
would you?

957
01:45:08,981 --> 01:45:10,179
Come here.

958
01:45:14,611 --> 01:45:16,983
I must release you.

959
01:45:27,875 --> 01:45:28,875
Fuck!

960
01:46:35,192 --> 01:46:36,437
Not anymore.

961
01:46:54,294 --> 01:46:55,294
Kill him.

962
01:46:55,504 --> 01:46:57,212
Wait! I owe you, man.

963
01:46:57,631 --> 01:46:59,125
I got two new hands, Blade.

964
01:46:59,550 --> 01:47:01,430
I don't know which one
to use to kill you with!

965
01:48:46,073 --> 01:48:48,065
I'm really going
to enjoy this now.

966
01:49:40,335 --> 01:49:42,292
Let's do this.

967
01:50:36,058 --> 01:50:37,682
You're too late, Blade.

968
01:50:57,204 --> 01:50:58,746
My turn.

969
01:51:25,107 --> 01:51:27,479
Look at you.
You're a little bitch.

970
01:51:29,319 --> 01:51:30,861
What, your serum?

971
01:51:31,280 --> 01:51:32,822
It can't help you now, stud.

972
01:51:40,205 --> 01:51:41,486
Nice shot.

973
01:52:13,614 --> 01:52:17,148
Some motherfuckers are always
trying to ice-skate uphill.

974
01:52:59,284 --> 01:53:01,241
Let's get out of here.

975
01:53:36,864 --> 01:53:40,315
I need to get back to the lab
if I'm going to cure you.

976
01:53:42,286 --> 01:53:43,994
It's not over.

977
01:53:44,413 --> 01:53:45,788
You keep your cure.

978
01:53:46,915 --> 01:53:48,409
There's still a war going on...

979
01:53:48,834 --> 01:53:50,791
and I have a job to do.

980
01:53:52,087 --> 01:53:53,795
You want to help...

981
01:53:54,214 --> 01:53:56,337
make me a better serum.
